                    {
                        "translation_id": "7717685e-af8e-48bf-8ec6-8ef409c4df78",
                        "source_entry_id": "2474917a-e412-3556-a101-4e59bf7e5ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "373390c9-7e87-3b6f-aabb-abd584905d88",
                        "source_sense_description": "Darstellung eines Gefühls, Gegenstandes oder Ereignisses auf eine lebendige, vergegenwärtigende Weise",
                        "target_lang_word": "portrayal",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "portrayal",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be337732-0e81-3bf5-9f4f-a10239c5817f",
                                        "entry_id": "a2d5dbd3-8f6c-3474-870b-dc5ee29487f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of portraying."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3eb64d9d-70f3-3412-afc5-80b60284c16c",
                                        "entry_id": "a2d5dbd3-8f6c-3474-870b-dc5ee29487f2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The result of portraying; a representation, description, or portrait."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7cdf6e7b-33ba-49db-b155-fb2124f694dd",
                                                "sense_id": "3eb64d9d-70f3-3412-afc5-80b60284c16c",
                                                "text": "1866, Charlotte Yonge, The Dove in the Eagle's Nest\nHe had already designed the portrayal of his father as the old white king, and himself as the young white king, in a series of woodcuts illustrating the narrative which culminated in the one romance of his life, ..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fd357dd-2d58-42be-b5b1-d6a062e215ec",
                                                "sense_id": "3eb64d9d-70f3-3412-afc5-80b60284c16c",
                                                "text": "1909, Arnold Bennett, Literary Taste\nFor days afterwards you will not be able to look upon a child without recalling Lamb's portrayal of the grace of childhood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48fd8393-c593-4f0a-bc15-3f2f7755a0c8",
                                                "sense_id": "3eb64d9d-70f3-3412-afc5-80b60284c16c",
                                                "text": "Dickens was the quintessential actor, luxuriating in the portrayal of his idiosyncratic characters. In contrast, more than a characterist, Poe was above all a wonderfully musical reader, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9677532b-0ab2-478e-85cd-92672f89cf13",
                                                "sense_id": "3eb64d9d-70f3-3412-afc5-80b60284c16c",
                                                "text": "Images of Dutchness in American visual culture and literature during the nineteenth century differed radically between portrayals of the Netherlands Dutch and those of the American Dutch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ef7f523-6a38-4241-98a7-6105c754d886",
                        "source_entry_id": "2474917a-e412-3556-a101-4e59bf7e5ad3",
                        "source_sense_id": "373390c9-7e87-3b6f-aabb-abd584905d88",
                        "source_sense_description": "Darstellung eines Gefühls, Gegenstandes oder Ereignisses auf eine lebendige, vergegenwärtigende Weise",
                        "target_lang_word": "depiction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "depiction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8151fc8b-8065-3380-a5e3-8aae75d8f6b6",
                                        "entry_id": "a42d98fb-8d36-3577-8353-8aa53e0f1a82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lifelike image of something, either verbal or visual."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b2fb9bf-e320-4c34-b122-53c7dd6a3f42",
                                                "sense_id": "8151fc8b-8065-3380-a5e3-8aae75d8f6b6",
                                                "text": "If Demandt's essay served as a strident example of the German desire for normalcy, a more subtle example was provided by a brief allohistorical depiction of a Nazi victory in World War II written by German historian Michael Salewski in 1999."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1020f3a9-5231-3ff8-8e03-db989ad80bbb",
                                        "entry_id": "a42d98fb-8d36-3577-8353-8aa53e0f1a82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A drawing or painting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cefa492a-1f45-371f-b69c-1f74a66aec6a",
                                        "entry_id": "a42d98fb-8d36-3577-8353-8aa53e0f1a82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A representation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "488cbe1a-1552-3f1f-8975-4f833f27fd10",
                                        "entry_id": "a42d98fb-8d36-3577-8353-8aa53e0f1a82",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of depicting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a84e025-6737-4e94-87f3-5a33e9deee1e",
                                                "sense_id": "488cbe1a-1552-3f1f-8975-4f833f27fd10",
                                                "text": "It is nevertheless true that, whereas the teaching of music and literature is established on a scientific basis, the art of depiction is still taught in a primitive and inefficient way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1d3fb34-3b71-4a48-9cf3-f82cd53ec156",
                                                "sense_id": "488cbe1a-1552-3f1f-8975-4f833f27fd10",
                                                "text": "But since \"realism\" or representational depiction is itself a mode of art, it can never escape some degree of formal removal from the raw data of experience; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "473694fa-2413-4ba2-a97a-ba0883543ee9",
                                                "sense_id": "488cbe1a-1552-3f1f-8975-4f833f27fd10",
                                                "text": "As previously described, depiction is a unique type of visual representation defined by both seeing the activities/marks that constitute the depiction whilst also seeing the object of the depiction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
